+#### End-Turn Token Usage (Unstable)
+The Agent **MAY** include `usage` on an idle `state_update` to report token usage for completed foreground work. It is not part of the `session/prompt` response and is distinct from the current context-window and cumulative cost information in [`usage_update`](#session-usage-updates).
+```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "session/update",
  "params": {
    "sessionId": "sess_abc123def456",
    "update": {
      "sessionUpdate": "state_update",
      "state": "idle",
      "stopReason": "end_turn",
      "usage": {
        "totalTokens": 150,
        "inputTokens": 100,
        "outputTokens": 50
      }
    }
  }
}
```
+`usage` is optional and nullable; omission and `null` both mean no usage was reported. No capability is required. Clients without this experimental field ignore it, and Clients that recognize it discard malformed usage rather than rejecting the idle transition. Sending usage does not establish that the Client displays it. See [Experimental Features and Negotiation](/protocol/v2/extensibility#experimental-features-and-negotiation).
