+Agents report `unknown` on actual loss of observability, not merely after silence. Clients must no longer present a prior `running` or `requires_action` as confirmed live activity, though they may retain the last-known state for context. A subsequent `running`, `requires_action`, or `idle` replaces `unknown` for the same session. `unknown` is neither a work outcome nor a closure or cancellation, and does not resolve pending requests or automatically revoke child mutation capabilities; the Agent updates those capabilities separately if a control becomes unavailable.
 Background activity **MAY** continue and emit other `session/update` notifications while the Agent reports `idle`. These notifications do not change the state.
